I read this somewhere and it worked for me (in 3.1.2, I think):

































On the wizard level go and stand on the stairs. Wait for the Wizard to
appear. Throw a potion of paralysis at him. Do NOT kill him. Go up
stairs. Never return to that level (unless you have another potion).

This works because the code knows that he is paralysed, so he doesn't
keep on popping-up on all the different levels. But the time-out on his
paralysis is only checked when you are on the same level as him. So if
you never return to that level, he will never wake up/unparalyse.

Of course, this may have changed in newer versions.

